{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And HaShem appeared to him, etc., and he built there, etc.</b> The intent of the verse is to make known the surpassing love of Abraham for his Creator: for HaShem revealed Himself to him and gave him the good tidings of seed and of the giving of the land, yet he did not regard the tidings of these two blessings as anything comparable to his joy at the revelation of the Shechinah, may He be blessed, to him — fulfilling what is said (Psalms 16:11): ״שׂוֹבַע שְׂמָחוֹת אֶת פָּנֶיךָ״. And this is its saying <b>and he built an altar to HaShem who appeared to him</b> — here he explained the cause of his joy for which he built the altar, namely on account of His appearing, may He be blessed, to him. Understand this. And this is a sign for his children: how many among them pushed off the longing for seed in favor of the longing for Torah and commandments. Go out and learn from ben Azzai (Yevamot 63b) in his argument: ״And what shall I do, for my soul craves Torah?״"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:46.013161192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}